---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/`;
---
<BaseLayout title="Medway Genealogy Research" description="Evidence-led research into the Medway / Meadway family of Dorset and Southampton, with primary sources, hypotheses and archive priorities.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">Dorset · family history · working archive</div>
    <h1>The Medway / Meadway research desk</h1>
    <p class="lead">A public working archive for tracing the family from Southampton and Hamworthy back through Poole, Lytchett Minster, Purbeck and the earlier Dorset surname network. The site records what the sources actually say, what is strongly suggested, what has been excluded, and which records could change the story next.</p>
    <p class="hero-links"><a class="button" href={`${base}family-tree/`}>View the family tree</a><a class="button secondary" href={`${base}research/latest-findings/`}>Latest findings</a><a class="button secondary" href={`${base}research/project-review/`}>Read the evidence review</a></p>
  </section>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Research rule:</strong> a genuine record for a person of the right name is not automatically evidence that the person belongs in the direct pedigree. Identity between records must be proved or clearly graded as a hypothesis.
  </div>

  <h2>Current position</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <article class="card">
      <span class="status proved">Documented anchor</span>
      <h3>James Medway, 1800</h3>
      <p>James, son of Matthew and Mary Medway, was baptised at Poole St James on 19 August 1800. The project line runs forward through Hamworthy and Southampton to the present family.</p>
      <p><a href={`${base}research/direct-line/`}>Follow the direct line →</a></p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <span class="status strong">Strong leading candidate</span>
      <h3>Mary Galley of Lytchett Minster</h3>
      <p>Mary, daughter of William Galley, baptised in 1760 is now the strongest candidate for Matthew's wife. The case is strengthened by a Galley network already spanning Lytchett and Hamworthy before her birth.</p>
      <p><a href={`${base}research/mary-galley/`}>Review the Mary Galley case →</a></p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <span class="status open">Central open question</span>
      <h3>Matthew's origins</h3>
      <p>The West Lulworth baptism of Matthew, son of John and Elizabeth, on 8 November 1758 is real. What is still missing is the bridge proving that child became the adult found at Hamworthy by 1781.</p>
      <p><a href={`${base}research/early-line/`}>Explore the earlier Dorset evidence →</a></p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <h2>Research library</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <article class="card"><h3>Family tree</h3><p>An evidence-graded visual tree including the established nineteenth- and twentieth-century ancestors, the Mary Galley research branch and the earlier Medway hypotheses.</p><p><a href={`${base}family-tree/`}>Open family tree →</a></p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Comprehensive review</h3><p>The consolidated chronology, corrections, exclusions, competing identities and open links from the project audit.</p><p><a href={`${base}research/project-review/`}>Open review →</a></p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Latest findings</h3><p>The 10–12 September additions: Cattistock land tax, naval-victualling research, Mary Cole probate and the 1749 Gally lease.</p><p><a href={`${base}research/latest-findings/`}>Open latest findings →</a></p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Evidence inventory</h3><p>A source-audit register for the primary images and key derivative records, including what each can and cannot establish.</p><p><a href={`${base}research/evidence-inventory/`}>Browse evidence →</a></p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Matthew the victualler</h3><p>Testing the 1781 occupational description against Navy and Victualling Board records without assuming that “victualler” means naval contractor.</p><p><a href={`${base}research/naval-victualling/`}>Read naval research →</a></p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Richard Meadway at Cattistock</h3><p>Three land-tax assessments place Richard at Cattistock in 1780–82. He remains a separate collateral lead until a relationship is found.</p><p><a href={`${base}research/cattistock-land-tax/`}>Read land-tax analysis →</a></p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Archive priorities</h3><p>The records most likely to distinguish candidates: Hill case, death certificate, settlement records, Bartlett probate, Herston deeds, Christopher probate and Gally leases.</p><p><a href={`${base}research/research-priorities/`}>Plan the next searches →</a></p></article>
  </div>

  <h2>Evidence standard</h2>
  <p>The major project audit recovered 429 distinct image files after exact-byte deduplication, with targeted close examination recorded for the most consequential material. Original registers, wills, militia lists, court papers, leases and probate documents take priority over derivative indexes or user-created family-tree links.</p>
  <p><a href={`${base}research/method/`}>Read the evidence method and coverage statement →</a></p>

  <h2>What is not yet a proved pedigree</h2>
  <p>The current evidence does not yet prove that Matthew of Hamworthy was the West Lulworth child baptised in 1758; that the relevant John was the 1734 Pimperne groom or the Swanage child of 1710/11; that Matthew of Herston was Matthias, son of Richard the curate; or that the curate belongs to a particular reconstructed Askerswell household. Those are the questions the archive plan is designed to solve.</p>
</BaseLayout>
